# Everything the scaffold generates or holds in confidence.
#
# This directory used to be ignored in full, which was right while it was
# scratch and wrong once it became something to deploy: Render builds from a
# repository, and a path git does not track is a path no host can fetch.
#
# So the source is tracked and these are not:
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
*.log

# `bag init` writes a v3 keystore and a .env.local holding WALLET_PASSWORD and
# provider API keys. An earlier scaffold was left in a temp directory with both
# in it; neither belongs in a repository either.
.studio/

# Carries the AWS account id. Not a password, and not something to publish in a
# repository that is going to be read by judges.
**/agentcore/aws-targets.json
